Generate a standalone C reproducer that triggers this vulnerability:

File: bfd/coff64-rs6000.c
Line: 1689
Function: xcoff64_ppc_relocate_section
Bug type: out-of-bounds-read
CWE: CWE-125
Explanation: The bounds check uses 'if (address > input_section->size) abort();' allowing address == input_section->size. Subsequent reads via bfd_get_16/32/64 at 'location = contents + address' will read past the end of the contents buffer when address == size.

